included. Source copied on 2026-09-13.

The separately built screen/panel.c and screen/qpic.h are GPL-3.0-or-later,
including adapted DRM code from https://github.com/amenekowo/mu5250_tweaking.
See screen/LICENSE and screen/NOTICE. The root MIT license does not relicense
these GPL files. The GNU Unifont OTF font uses SIL OFL 1.1; see screen/FONT-LICENSE
and screen/FONT-COPYING. Dependencies retain their own respective licenses.

The DevUI renderer is adapted from 33333s/u60pro-devui (MIT); its copyright
and dependency licenses are preserved in screen/THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.

vendor/tiny_http is tiny_http 0.12.0 (https://github.com/tiny-http/tiny-http,
MIT OR Apache-2.0; its license texts are kept in that directory) with resource
limits added for the agent's HTTP server. The changes are listed in
vendor/tiny_http/OPENUI-PATCH.md and marked in each modified file.

lpac (https://github.com/estkme-group/lpac, v2.3.0 with the patches in
scripts/lpac-patches/), deployed as /data/bin/lpac for eSIM management, is a separate
program under AGPL-3.0-only (libeuicc LGPL-2.1-only, cJSON MIT); see licenses/lpac/.
The MIT-licensed agent starts it and talks to it over standard input and output.
The dashboard's QR decoder is jsQR (Apache-2.0), shipped with its licence.
The eSIM root certificates in agent/certs/ are the public GSMA CI certificates.

The core program attached to releases as `mihomo` is GPL-3.0. scripts/prepare-mihomo.py
names the source repository and commit it is built from, and the changes in
scripts/mihomo-patches/ are GPL-3.0 as well; the root MIT license does not relicense them.
